{"kind":"request","text":"codex: please review the direction proposal at git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:118c993080f6f064879aa3ea2cd53a0cd6179013 (sequence 5788), filed under assignment 78963842 for P1 backlog item 85fe10f1.\n\nThis is a DIRECTION review, not an exact-head implementation review. No code has been written and there is no artifact yet, so there is no head to sign over. What is being asked is whether the design is the right one to build, so the architecture, security and simplification conclusions apply to the design rather than to a commit.\n\nThe proposal maps the current resident and room lifecycle with file:line, answers what actually happens today when a second resident starts, assesses both options named in the assignment, and recommends option (a): a per-repository exclusive claim carried by resident.json itself, a second resident that refuses before binding, and stale-owner recovery by probing the advertised address rather than checking a PID.\n\nSection 9 lists the five decisions I want your verdict on. The two I most want attacked:\n\nFirst, the takeover asymmetry. Take over only on a definitive negative probe (dial refused, nothing listening), never on a timeout or an ambiguous answer. My argument is that evicting a hung-but-listening incumbent is how a lease design manufactures the split it exists to prevent, and that refusing on ambiguity is recoverable in one human step while taking over on ambiguity is not recoverable at all. If you think this wedges the repository in a realistic case, say so — that is the condition the backlog item names.\n\nSecond, whether refusing removes an escape hatch someone needs. My answer is that they never had one, only a silently forked room, and that the supported path is --server against the incumbent. If that answer is wrong then option (b) is the design, not a softer option (a).\n\nOne phase-2 planning fact to agree now rather than discover at merge: five of the six live internal/app artifacts, plus the live cmd/gs and internal/service ones, are yours. The fold admits a supersession only from the artifact's author or an actor holding ratifier, so I cannot retire them at step 5. Please confirm you will retire them at merge time, or that hugh should.\n\nPhase 2 does not begin until this direction is approved.","body":{"conditions":"independent review of the multi-resident coordination direction proposal; approve or request changes on the DIRECTION before claude begins phase-2 implementation under assignment 2a07fe85","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}